{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor completed the minimum safety chain: current bleeding/pain/systemic symptoms were repeatedly triaged, uncertain ultrasound prognosis was not overcalled, medication confusion was routed to the original obstetric team with no self-adjustment, and follow-up timing/ED triggers were made executable. The strongest non-overlapping high-order completion was repair of the actual progesterone/Duphaston execution chain after missed doses, including same-day original-hospital verification and a concrete q8h schedule with patient teach-back. HO1 was only partial because much of the ambiguous-inpatient-vs-discharge injection verification overlapped with the required medication reconciliation and was not distinctly completed as a separate high-order action. With no responsibility-chain error and one completed high-order point, but not two, the trajectory is Strong rather than Perfect.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00194",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave an executable transition plan covering medication, injection, symptom monitoring, and 3-7 day obstetric follow-up.",
        "quote": "药接上了、针打上了、时间表排好了、急诊门槛也记清了"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00184",
        "explanation": "The patient demonstrated teach-back of emergency triggers and follow-up timing.",
        "quote": "要是变红多了、痛厉害、头晕发烧流水，我就直接急诊不等了"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00212",
        "explanation": "A non-urgent follow-up question about comorbidities remained open, making this a safe open transition rather than a fully closed episode.",
        "quote": "我要不要特别跟产科说我有乙肝大三阳"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The core episode had a safe, traceable plan: continue verified q8h Duphaston without doubling, return to the original hospital for daily progesterone injection, monitor clear ED triggers, and arrange obstetric follow-up within 3-7 days. The final patient message left a non-urgent comorbidity-follow-up clarification open, but the responsible service and next contact path were already established.",
    "label": "valid_open",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00194",
        "explanation": "The plan was converted into concrete medication timing, injection continuation, monitoring, and follow-up actions.",
        "quote": "今晚和明天就按这个方案执行"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00033",
        "explanation": "The doctor avoided falsely declaring stability and tied prognosis to symptoms, fetal cardiac activity, and follow-up ultrasound.",
        "quote": "不能简单说“已经稳定”"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00168",
        "explanation": "The doctor integrated the line doctor's confirmation and the patient's afternoon dosing time into a continuing schedule.",
        "quote": "从今天下午这一片开始对时"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00092",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave clear escalation criteria for dangerous bleeding, pain, and hemodynamic symptoms.",
        "quote": "直接去急诊"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00092",
        "explanation": "The doctor adapted to access barriers by specifying the original hospital route, backup location, and documents to bring.",
        "quote": "挂不上就去原来住院的那个病区护士站"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "excellent",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "good",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "good",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "excellent",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "excellent"
  },
